    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T00:06:52Z",
    "body": "**Hands-on check on macOS, release build of this branch.**\n\n- Panels… (View group) → **Machines** opens a \"machines\" tab next to \"properties\". It shows \"10 machines\" and a Refresh button.\n- The list shows each machine's kind, axes and unit, e.g. `Tormach 770MX (ML) (mill, XYZ, inch)`. With nothing selected it reads \"Select a machine to see its properties.\"\n- Selecting **Tormach 770MX (ML)** shows \"built-in\" and **Validation: passes**, with the General and Axes groups.\n  - General: model, vendor, kind mill, inch, degrees, 1 spindle.\n  - Axes: X ±14 in at 450 in/min, Y ±7.5 in at 450, Z ±13.25 in at 420. These match the operator's manual figures in the .mch.\n\n**Cosmetic, for the maintainer:** the Axes group lists the axes as **Z, Y, X**, the reverse of the usual X, Y, Z order. Not blocking.\n\nThe refusal case (an invalid `.mch` loaded through \"Load other\") was not exercised by hand. It is pinned by the `machine_library` and `machines_pane` tests.\n\n**Gate:** upstream/main merged (clean), then `scripts/gate.sh quick`. app and post are green. The remaining reds also fail on upstream main:\n- `swarf_pose_continuity`, fixed by #351;\n- the GPU headless tests (`headless_run_succeeds`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
